      "claim": "A pyrazolopyrimidinone analogue achieved 34% oral bioavailability, but this is a conventional drug-like molecule and does not represent the query's extreme physicochemical profile.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C01"],
      "claim": "Elagolix is reported to have good oral bioavailability, but as a smaller ionizable drug it is not analogous to the query's extreme lipophilicity and lack of ionizable groups.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C14"],
      "claim": "The active metabolite of nabumetone has 38% absolute bioavailability, but this is a low-molecular-weight, moderately lipophilic molecule, not transferable to the query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
